invariant: INV-17
file: src/chacha20_avx512.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: row_pass loses its noinline, so the pinned clang inlines it into
  chacha20_avx512_xor. Its reads of the input words then let the compiler
  keep the key the entry loaded in a register, and gcc 13 saved a copy of
  that register in the entry's frame, which no wipe names. Every byte the
  kernel writes is still right. The script compiles the kernel for x86-64
  and requires chacha20_avx512_xor to call row_pass.

--- old
static __attribute__((noinline)) void row_pass(const uint32_t words[16], uint32_t counter,
--- new
static void row_pass(const uint32_t words[16], uint32_t counter,
